    "description": "Hand-curated, significance-based candidate list for the Milestones lane. Not a SPARQL dump like the sibling events-*.raw.json files — this lane's selection and categorization is curated by hand and verified against live Wikidata per item. Originally 121 entries across the first 10 categories; merged with a second AI-sourced candidate list whose QIDs were almost entirely wrong (83 of 94 candidate ids resolved to an unrelated Wikidata item) — every new entry was re-resolved to its correct QID by name, and any candidate with no matching Wikidata item or no live Wikidata date-property claim was dropped rather than guessed. That second list also introduced 10 new categories, folded into meta.categories below since the per-category color-legend cost was negligible. A third batch of 16 entries (of 20 candidates — 4 dropped for no live date-property claim: Germ theory of disease, CRISPR-Cas method, Discovery of nuclear fission, X-ray) was added the same way, this time hand-searched against Wikidata directly rather than AI-recalled. year/month are no longer curator-authored here — fetchMilestonesEnrichment resolves them live per QID (see queries/milestones-enrichment.ts's DATE_PROPERTIES), same sourcing Conflicts already uses for its dates.",
